From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:31:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: skip the motion distance when the delta movement
 instance is unchanged

ServerEntity#sendChanges compared the delta movement with the last sent one on
every sync tick. The game reuses the same Vec3 when nothing moved, and the
distance of an instance to itself is 0, which never triggers a packet, so the
distance is not computed in that case.

Behaviour: identical.

Ported from Leaf/SparklyPaper "Skip distanceToSqr call in ServerEntity#sendChanges
if the delta movement hasn't changed" by MrPowerGamerBR <git@mrpowergamerbr.com>.
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerEntity.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerEntity.java
index e46f95b19da1c14f240ec6697f22b5e220e0a835..a08968dc0f1bf501de8f80b0d6a3c6f270461e91 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerEntity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerEntity.java
@@ -192,7 +192,8 @@ public class ServerEntity {
 
                 if (this.entity.needsSync || this.trackDelta || this.entity instanceof LivingEntity livingEntity && livingEntity.isFallFlying()) {
                     Vec3 movement = this.entity.getDeltaMovement();
-                    double diff = movement.distanceToSqr(this.lastSentMovement);
+                    // Leaf port - the very same Vec3 instance has a distance of 0 and never changes anything (Leaf/SparklyPaper "Skip distanceToSqr call in ServerEntity#sendChanges", MrPowerGamerBR)
+                    double diff = movement == this.lastSentMovement ? 0.0 : movement.distanceToSqr(this.lastSentMovement);
                     if (diff > 1.0E-7 || diff > 0.0 && movement.lengthSqr() == 0.0) {
                         this.lastSentMovement = movement;
                         if (this.entity instanceof AbstractHurtingProjectile projectile) {
